## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical implementation of policy-driven AI in multi-tenant analytics, including query rewriting, PII handling, budget-aware gating, KB grounding, and end-to-end auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Fine-grained access policies (RLS), prompt hygiene
- Query rewriting to enforce security
- Budget gating and cost controls
- KB grounding with Cognitive Search
- Auditing to Data Lake and PKI isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo function to rewrite a SQL prompt with tenant policy
function rewriteQuery(sql, policy) {
  // append where clause from policy
  const where = `(${policy.whereClause})`;
  return sql.replace(/WHERE/i, where);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy coverage and false positives?
- How would you scale policy updates without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
To assess hands-on Azure AI wiring for accessibility use cases, including voice input, multilingual output, and privacy controls, all grounded in a managed KB.

## Key Concepts
- Azure API Management as a gate
- Azure OpenAI with grounding to a versioned KB in Blob via Cognitive Search
- Azure Speech to Text and Text to Speech
- Per-tenant language preferences
- PII redaction and interaction logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example flow tying services together
async function handleQuery(audioBlob, language) {
  const text = await speechToText(audioBlob, language);
  const answer = await openai.chat({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: text }] });
  const tts = await textToSpeech(answer.choices[0].message.content, language);
  return tts;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model per-tenant language settings in Cosmos DB?
- What are the trade-offs between cloud TTS and on-device synthesis for accessibility tasks?

## Why This Is Asked

